<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mirza Abu Bakr Dughlat</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1514</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mirza Abu Bakr <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dughlat">Dughlat</a> (died c. 1514) was an amir of the Dughlat clan who built an independent realm in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashgar">Kashgar</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yarkand">Yarkand</a> and Khotan in the late 15th century, nominally within <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moghulistan">Moghulistan</a>. He was remembered as a harsh ruler and a builder of fortifications. In 1514 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan-said-khan">Sultan Said Khan</a> drove him out of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashgaria">Kashgaria</a>, founding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yarkent-khanate">Yarkent Khanate</a>, and he died soon after while in flight.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mirza-abu-bakr-dughlat.jpg" alt="Mirza Abu Bakr Dughlat" width="320" height="531" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nand Gwaliori · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1494-Abubekr_Duglat_attempting_unsuccessfully_to_take_Uzgend_th.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
